<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">health</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">health</ansi> (Hitpoints/HP) stat represents how much damage you can take.

Health will change color to reflect how good/bad your health state is:

<ansi fg="health-100">100%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-90">90%-99%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-80">80%-89%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-70">70%-79%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-60">60%-69%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-50">50%-59%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-40">40%-49%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-30">30%-39%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-20">20%-29%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-10">10%-19%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-0">0%-9%</ansi>
<ansi fg="health-dead">dead</ansi>

While you are wounded, healing stops at your wound limit, below your
maximum: <ansi fg="command">status</ansi> shows it as <ansi fg="command">12/16 (limit 13)</ansi> (<ansi fg="command">help wounds</ansi>).

Out of a fight you slowly regain health and mana; so do your companions,
while you're logged in. A finished night at an inn restores you all to
full. Companions keep their health when you log out, so it's the same
when you come back (<ansi fg="command">help readiness</ansi>).

At <ansi fg="red">0 HP</ansi>, you will drop to the floor and slowly bleed out.

At <ansi fg="red">-10 HP</ansi>, you will die. When you die, all gear you posess drops to the ground.

Maximum health comes from a base, your archetype's gains through level
{{ config "GamePlay.Progression.HPFullLevels" }}, then a smaller gain per later level in proportion to your archetype, plus
{{ config "GamePlay.Progression.HPPerVitality" }} HP per adjusted Vitality and health bonuses. See <ansi fg="command">help progression</ansi>.

